  "conclusions": [
    "Dynamic compression remains accurate across all three windows: mean BIQAE ES compression bias -0.106/-0.132/-0.150 bp.",
    "Improved compression does not guarantee market improvement: BIQAE heldout ES changes -1.712/+2.162/+8.074 bp vs original64 across windows.",
    "Window 2 retains 11.762 bp raw LP gap and 0.270 L2 weight distance; exact raw gradient also has 11.569 bp gap under validation-selected learning rate 0.03 and 120 steps. Therefore compression accuracy passes but universal optimization acceptance fails.",
    "Annual 2011-2025 BIQAE at 10 bp per traded dollar: annualized return 13.041%, volatility 15.769%, maximum drawdown -30.542%, daily ES97.5 3.069%; raw LP achieves return13.680%, drawdown-27.717%, ES3.022%. No business advantage over exact LP.",
    "Annual paths use one fixed training seed per year, historical industry returns, annual rebalancing and drifting weights. Rebalance weight constraints are satisfied; intra-year drift is not continuously constrained. No claim of statistical seed certification, tradable instrument execution or quantum speedup."
  ]
